Subject: ubox: write the boot's backlog to the persistent log file

The logfile follower asks logd for no backlog, so the persistent log
file starts each boot at the moment the follower attached and misses
the kernel and early-init lines before it. At boot, ask for the whole
ring buffer, which then holds this boot alone.

Start9 downstream patch (start-technologies projects/start-wrt).
Applies to: openwrt v25.12.6

--- a/package/system/ubox/files/log.init
+++ b/package/system/ubox/files/log.init
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@
 	procd_open_instance logfile
 	procd_set_param command "$PROG" -f -F "$log_file" -p "$pid_file"
 	[ -n "${log_size}" ] && procd_append_param command -S "$log_size"
+	[ "$_BOOT" = "1" ] && procd_append_param command -l 1000000
 	procd_close_instance
 }
 
